"""Build the local delivery report from measured conversion and browser results."""
import html
import json
import pathlib

root = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / 'public/images/cinematic hero section'
manifest = json.loads((root / 'manifest.json').read_text())
qa = json.loads((root / 'browser-validation.json').read_text())
rows = []
performance = []
media = []
for name, sequence in manifest['sequences'].items():
    rows.append(f"<tr><th>{name.title()}</th><td>{sequence['frameCount']:,}</td><td>{sequence['width']} × {sequence['height']}</td><td>{sequence['fps']}</td><td>{sequence['quality']}</td><td>{sequence['totalBytes']:,} bytes ({sequence['totalBytes']/1e6:.2f} MB)</td><td>{sequence['averageFrameBytes']/1000:.2f} KB</td></tr>")
    result = qa['variants'][name]
    performance.append(f"<li>{name.title()}: {result['drawCount']} Canvas draws in the scripted traversal; p95 synchronous draw call {result['drawP95Milliseconds']:.2f} ms; {result['requests']} frame requests, including revisits/cancellations; {result['longTaskCount']} browser long tasks (maximum {result['longestTaskMilliseconds']:.1f} ms). No page errors or document overflow. Frame/cache/concurrency assertions passed.</li>")
    media.append(f'<article><h3>{name.title()}</h3><video controls preload="metadata" src="{name}-scroll-recording.webm"></video><p><a href="{name}-scroll-recording.webm">Open recording</a></p><img src="{name}-canvas-hero.png" alt="{name} homepage with Canvas background"></article>')
report = f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>RESTRO — Continuous Canvas sequence report</title>
<style>body{{margin:0;background:#12100d;color:#eee8dc;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}}main{{max-width:1150px;margin:auto;padding:40px 24px}}h1,h2,h3{{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;line-height:1.2}}h1{{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,56px)}}h2{{margin-top:42px;color:#dfb87d}}a{{color:#dfb87d}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}}td,th{{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff24}}.table{{overflow:auto}}.media{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:24px}}video,img{{width:100%;height:auto;max-height:700px;object-fit:contain;background:#090807}}code{{overflow-wrap:anywhere}}.muted{{color:#bcb4a6}}</style>
<main><p class="muted">25 November 2026 · Local production verification</p><h1>RESTRO continuous cinematic frames</h1>
<p>Implemented a fixed full-screen Canvas that follows native homepage scrolling in both directions, freezes when scrolling stops and interpolates through measured section anchors. Existing glass surfaces, typography, navigation, forms, carousels, grid and mobile layouts are preserved.</p>
<h2>Measured delivery assets</h2><div class="table"><table><tr><th>Sequence</th><th>Frames</th><th>Dimensions</th><th>FPS</th><th>Quality</th><th>Total size</th><th>Average frame</th></tr>{''.join(rows)}</table></div>
<p>Combined sequences: <strong>{manifest['totalBytes']:,} bytes / {manifest['totalBytes']/1e6:.2f} MB / {manifest['totalBytes']/1048576:.2f} MiB</strong>. Individual nonanimated lossy WebP images, FFmpeg libwebp, compression level 6, Lanczos scaling, no crop. Indexes begin at 1 and end at the actual frame count.</p>
<p>FFprobe verified the original 1920 × 1080 H.264 video at 30 FPS, {manifest['duration']} seconds / 1,675 source frames; the container is {manifest['containerDuration']} seconds because of its audio tail. Both outputs cover the complete picture duration with 16:9 aspect ratio. Mobile resamples the full footage to 24 FPS. Original {manifest['source']['bytes']:,}-byte MP4 preserved. SHA-256: <code>{manifest['source']['sha256']}</code>.</p>
<p>Every generated frame was decoded with Pillow and checked for dimensions, nonanimated format, contiguous names and unexpected black images (mean luminance &lt;2); all 3,015 passed. FFmpeg logs preserve extraction order. Representative quality comparisons at 70/75/80 retained visible lighting and shadow detail; lower qualities reduced both size and measured source similarity. The requested settings were retained. These files total more than the previous inter-frame compressed MP4s, as expected for independent images.</p>
<p><a href="manifest.json">Manifest</a> · <a href="source-inspection.json">FFprobe output</a> · <a href="quality-comparison.json">Quality metrics</a> · <a href="browser-validation.json">Browser results</a></p><img src="quality-comparison.jpg" alt="Representative source frames compared at qualities 70, 75 and 80">
<h2>Loading and rendering</h2><ul><li>One selected variant at activation: below 768px uses mobile; otherwise desktop. Resizing retains that variant to avoid a second sequence download.</li><li>Manifest supplies actual counts/dimensions/FPS. Piecewise section interpolation maps scroll position to seconds, then an exact frame index. Small scrolls expose intermediate frames; the short desktop footer reserves up to 250px for closing movement.</li><li>Exact target first, then up to 12 frames ahead and four behind in the current direction. Reversing reprioritizes the queue. Stale requests are aborted. Mobile allows three concurrent downloads; desktop four.</li><li>Decoded bitmap cache: mobile 20 (about 39.6 MiB RGBA); desktop 24 (84.4 MiB), excluding Canvas, browser overhead and in-flight decoding. Farthest frames are closed on eviction. HTTP compressed caching remains browser-managed.</li><li>Passive native scroll events schedule a single requestAnimationFrame; no idle rendering loop or scroll interception. Only bitmap arrival, geometry or user events schedule work. No per-frame React render is needed.</li><li>The last successfully drawn picture stays visible until the exact target is ready. Resizing and cover drawing happen in the same task. Cover cropping preserves aspect ratio and the kitchen focal point. No scene crossfades, artificial zoom, slideshow or video element.</li><li>Reduced motion and Save-Data default to static imagery unless explicitly overridden. Existing persistent mode control remains. Form/dialog editing freezes movement. Manifest failures retain scene imagery; delayed frame loads hold the existing Canvas. Cleanup aborts requests, closes bitmaps and removes subscriptions on effect teardown.</li></ul>
<h2>Validation and performance</h2><p>Passed <code>npx tsc --noEmit</code>, <code>npm run lint</code> (zero warnings), <code>npm run build</code> (16 expected routes/paths), cinematic mapping checks and new loader tests for indexing, direction, cancellation, concurrency, eviction and disposal. The initial sandbox build failed because Turbopack’s CSS worker could not connect; the regular production build passed outside that sandbox.</p><ul>{''.join(performance)}</ul>
<p>Browser suite covered desktop 1440×900 and touch-enabled mobile 390×844, full forward/reverse sweeps, intermediate 10px scroll steps, interior motion across sections including footer, settled exact frame matching, no black Canvas samples, stopped-scroll freeze, static-mode download cancellation, single-variant loading, resize, client navigation, reduced-motion defaults, manifest failure and 900ms delayed image responses.</p>
<p class="muted">Draw-call timings measure synchronous JavaScript submission, not GPU completion or guaranteed display FPS. Traversal recordings use controlled scroll steps (~11 per second), with native wheel/touch smoke checks. Local results do not establish physical-device or WAN performance.</p>
<h2>Screen recordings</h2><div class="media">{''.join(media)}</div>
<h2>Remaining limitations</h2><p>Physical iOS/Android, Safari/Firefox, real network throttling, memory/GPU profiling and production-host cache headers remain unverified. Slow networks and large scroll jumps may hold the last picture while an uncached target loads. The landscape footage necessarily crops horizontally on portrait screens. Two failed attempts per unavailable frame retain the last successful picture; a new position requests a different frame. No deployment or source-video modification was performed.</p>
<p>All generated frames and delivery/QA outputs are stored under <code>{html.escape(str(root))}</code>. Source preparation and verification scripts remain under the project scripts directory. Project handoff updated in HANDOFF.md.</p></main></html>'''
(root / 'report.html').write_text(report, encoding='utf-8')
print(root / 'report.html')
